{"id": "len-3e-batch-read-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "number", "bits": 16, "value": 12, "hex": "0C 00", "meaning": "request data length L = 000CH for the batch read of JY997D56001-K p.19", "section": "p.19", "note": "The SAME request is 000CH = 12 bytes in binary and 0018H = 24 characters in ASCII. L counts wire units, never binary-equivalent bytes.", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "JY997D56001", "revision": "K"}
{"id": "len-3e-batch-read-ascii", "codec": "ascii", "op": "number", "bits": 16, "value": 24, "hex": "30 30 31 38", "meaning": "the same L, 0018H = 24 characters", "section": "p.19", "note": "Most significant digit first, uppercase, zero padded to 4 characters.", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "JY997D56001", "revision": "K"}
{"id": "serial-4e-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "number", "bits": 16, "value": 4660, "hex": "34 12", "meaning": "4E serial number 1234H, lower byte first", "section": "4.2 p.21", "note": "Paired with serial-4e-ascii: 34 12 and '1234' are the same value under each coding's own rule and are NOT hexlify() of one another.", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "SH(NA)-080956ENG", "revision": "M"}
{"id": "serial-4e-ascii", "codec": "ascii", "op": "number", "bits": 16, "value": 4660, "hex": "31 32 33 34", "meaning": "4E serial number 1234H, upper byte first", "section": "4.2 p.21", "note": "'When sending the message in ASCII code, the serial No. is stored from the upper byte to the lower byte.'", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "SH(NA)-080956ENG", "revision": "M"}
{"id": "len-abnormal-3e-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "number", "bits": 16, "value": 11, "hex": "0B 00", "meaning": "L = 000BH, every abnormal 3E binary response", "note": "All 16 abnormal frames captured on the bench were exactly 20 bytes with L = 000BH and no command-defined trailer.", "provenance": "live", "cpu": "FX5U-32MT/DS", "firmware": "1.065", "measured": "2026-09-06"}
{"id": "f32-1234p5-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "number", "bits": 32, "value": 1150963712, "hex": "00 50 9A 44", "meaning": "IEEE-754 1234.5 as one 1402 double-word access point", "note": "Written to D104 as one dword point; read back raw as D104=5000H, D105=449AH. Low word first. High word first would give 8607918080.0.", "provenance": "live", "cpu": "FX5U-32MT/DS", "firmware": "1.065", "measured": "2026-09-06"}
{"id": "f32-1234p5-ascii", "codec": "ascii", "op": "number", "bits": 32, "value": 1150963712, "hex": "34 34 39 41 35 30 30 30", "meaning": "the same value, ASCII coding: high word first", "section": "10.1 (per-field headings pp.19, 21, 23, 24, 27, 28)", "note": "The binary/ASCII dword flip is exactly this pair. Same value, same call, one rule per codec, no word-order branch.", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "SH(NA)-080956ENG", "revision": "M"}
{"id": "f32-60p375-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "number", "bits": 32, "value": 1114734592, "hex": "00 80 71 42", "meaning": "IEEE-754 60.375 written to the live setpoint D0-D1", "note": "Read back bit-for-bit as D0=8000H, D1=4271H, and the running controller visibly reacted to the new setpoint.", "provenance": "live", "cpu": "FX5U-32MT/DS", "firmware": "1.065", "measured": "2026-09-06"}
{"id": "f32-60p0-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "number", "bits": 32, "value": 1114636288, "hex": "00 00 70 42", "meaning": "IEEE-754 60.0, the original D0-D1 setpoint, restored byte-identically", "provenance": "live", "cpu": "FX5U-32MT/DS", "firmware": "1.065", "measured": "2026-09-06"}
