{"id": "words-t100-t102-ascii", "codec": "ascii", "op": "words", "values": [4660, 2, 7663], "hex": "31 32 33 34 30 30 30 32 31 44 45 46", "meaning": "the same three words in ASCII coding", "section": "10.1 rule applied to the p.49 example", "note": "Four uppercase hex digits per point; the 2x length rule does hold for word data.", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "SH(NA)-080956ENG", "revision": "M"}
{"id": "words-f32-negative-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "words", "values": [59064, 51136], "hex": "B8 E6 C0 C7", "meaning": "D110, D111 -- the low then high half of IEEE-754 -98765.4375", "note": "Written as a plain 1401 two-word batch and read back as ONE 0403 dword point, which returned -98765.4375. The lower-numbered device holds the low word.", "provenance": "live", "cpu": "FX5U-32MT/DS", "firmware": "1.065", "measured": "2026-09-06"}
{"id": "bits-m100-m107-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "bits", "values": [false, false, false, true, false, false, true, true], "hex": "00 01 00 11", "meaning": "0401 bit-unit read of M100-M107, the manual's own worked response", "section": "4.1 p.47", "note": "Nibbles 0,0 / 0,1 / 0,0 / 1,1 -- first point in the HIGH nibble. This is the vector that fails if the packing order is reversed.", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "SH(NA)-080956ENG", "revision": "M"}
{"id": "bits-m100-m107-ascii", "codec": "ascii", "op": "bits", "values": [false, false, false, true, false, false, true, true], "hex": "30 30 30 31 30 30 31 31", "meaning": "the same eight points in ASCII coding: one character per point", "section": "p.40 rule applied to the p.47 example", "note": "Eight characters, not four bytes. The digits happen to read like the binary hex; they are 30H/31H characters.", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "SH(NA)-080956ENG", "revision": "M"}
{"id": "bits-m10-five-binary", "codec": "binary", "op": "bits", "values": [true, false, true, false, true], "hex": "10 10 10", "meaning": "five bit points from M10, binary: three bytes, trailing low nibble padded 0", "section": "p.40", "note": "'0 is shown when the number of points is an odd number.'", "provenance": "manual", "manual": "SH(NA)-080956ENG", "revision": "M"}
